A 1..=7 by 1..=7 convolution in device pixels. Kernel is rotated 180 degrees
as in SVG feConvolveMatrix. Unit lengths select bilinearly sampled offsets;
this is not an intermediate-image rescaling implementation.

Immutable filled region, shared on clone. Input winding/holes/self-intersections
are resolved by Lyon in f32; Boolean clipping then uses f64 polygons. This is
approximate polygon geometry, not exact curve algebra or a stroke outline.

```
use jadix_2d::*;
let shape = PathGeometry2D::from_path(&filled_rect(0., 0., 8., 8.), FillRule::NonZero,
    PathBooleanOptions::default()).unwrap();
let clip = PathGeometry2D::from_path(&filled_circle(4., 4., 4., 64), FillRule::NonZero,
    PathBooleanOptions::default()).unwrap();
let visible = shape.boolean(&clip, PathBooleanOp::Intersection,
    PathBooleanOptions::default()).unwrap();
let mut canvas = RasterCanvas::new_linear(8, 8);
canvas.set_fill("white");
visible.fill(&mut canvas);
```

Paint prepared colors, preserving caller state, CTM, alpha, clip/mask and
layer context. Outline text remains vector under arbitrary transforms;
atlas, SVG and bitmap text have the fixed prepared raster resolution.

Frozen commands and shared images/gradients/glyphs/subscenes. Recording does
not allocate a canvas bitmap, rasterize, tessellate or keep the callback.
It is an acyclic snapshot: children already exist before a parent is sealed.

```
use jadix_2d::{Canvas2D, RasterCanvas, Scene2D, SceneOptions};
let icon = Scene2D::record([24, 24], |c| {
    c.set_fill("#20a0ff");
    c.fill_rect(2., 2., 20., 20.);
}).unwrap();
let mut canvas = RasterCanvas::new_linear(64, 32);
for x in [4., 34.] {
    icon.draw(&mut canvas, SceneOptions {
        transform: [1., 0., 0., 1., x, 4.],
        ..Default::default()
    }).unwrap();
}
```

